  "cuts.col.speed_power": "Spd/Pwr",
  "help.art_library.p1": "Collections of ready-made artwork in folders. Hover a thumbnail to see it larger, click it to put it on the page. Add your selection to the chosen folder, or drop files onto the panel.",
  "help.art_library.p2": "Right-click an item to rename it, replace it with the selection, or delete it.",
  "help.art_library.title": "Art Library",
  "help.camera.p1": "Place a live or captured picture of the bed behind your design so artwork can be lined up with the material. It becomes active when a camera is set up.",
  "help.camera.title": "Camera Control",
  "help.canvas.p1": "Click a shape to select it. Shift adds to the selection, Ctrl and Shift removes. Drag a box from left to right to select what it encloses, from right to left to select what it touches.",
  "help.canvas.p2": "Scroll to zoom, hold the middle button or Space to pan. Arrow keys nudge the selection by the distances set in Settings.",
  "help.canvas.title": "The canvas",
  "help.console.p1": "The console shows what the machine says back and lets you type a command to send. It becomes active when a machine is connected.",
  "help.console.title": "Console",
  "help.cut_settings.p1": "All the settings of one layer: mode, speed, power, passes and more. Beginner mode in Settings hides the advanced tab.",
  "help.cut_settings.title": "Cut Settings",
  "help.cuts.p1": "Each layer is a colour with its own cut settings. Shapes take the settings of the layer they are on. Click a layer to make it current, double-click it to open all of its settings.",
  "help.cuts.p2": "Drag layers to change the order they are output in. The tick boxes switch output, visibility and air assist for a layer.",
  "help.cuts.title": "Cuts / Layers",
  "help.debug_off": "Debug log is off.",
  "help.debug_on": "Debug log is on.",
  "help.file_list.p1": "Lists the jobs stored in the controller of machines that keep files, so they can be run, uploaded or deleted.",
  "help.file_list.title": "File List",
  "help.general.p1": "Draw or import shapes, give each colour its cut settings in Cuts / Layers, then send the job to the laser.",
  "help.general.p2": "Press F1 with the pointer over a panel or a dialog to read about it. Settings and Edit Hotkeys are in the application bar and the File menu.",
  "help.general.title": "Getting started",
  "help.gweike.p1": "DarkBurn writes the files the Gweike software opens: DXF with a layer per material, G-code (.nc) and the .chf craft file. Map each layer to a material and a craft in the Gweike window.",
  "help.gweike.p2": "The card simulator plans the job and shows the time estimate. Nothing is sent to the machine. Direct control waits for a read-only capture on the real card (see docs/research/mlaser-rea-findings.md). The machine's own height follower, piercing and gas logic always stay in charge.",
  "help.gweike.title": "Gweike M3 Ultra",
  "help.hotkeys.p1": "Choose a command, press Set, then press the key combination you want. If another command already uses it you can take the key over.",
  "help.hotkeys.p2": "Hotkey sets can be exported to a file and imported on another computer.",
  "help.hotkeys.title": "Hotkeys",
  "help.laser.p1": "Start, pause and stop a job, frame it, or save it as a file. Start from chooses where the job is placed: at the page's own coordinates, at the laser's present position, or at a user origin.",
  "help.laser.p2": "Nothing here talks to a machine until you connect one.",
  "help.laser.title": "Laser",
  "help.library.p1": "A library keeps cut settings that worked, sorted by material, thickness and description. Assign an entry to put its settings on the current layer and link them, or create an entry from the layer you tuned.",
  "help.library.p2": "A linked layer shows which entry it follows. Deleting an entry unlinks its layers. Libraries are saved as files, one can be chosen for each machine.",
  "help.library.title": "Material library",
  "help.move.p1": "Jog the laser head by a set distance, go home, or set the origin. It becomes active when a machine is connected.",
  "help.move.title": "Move",
  "help.other_topics": "Other topics:",
  "help.settings.p1": "Settings are grouped by topic. They are saved as you change them. Units, speed units, snapping, nudge distances and the interface scale apply at once.",
  "help.settings.p2": "A shared defaults file lets a workshop give every computer the same starting settings.",
  "help.settings.title": "Settings",
  "help.shape_properties.p1": "Shows and changes everything about the selected shape: its name, layer, position, size, and for text the font and spacing.",
  "help.shape_properties.title": "Shape Properties",
  "help.support_saved": "Support data saved to",
  "help.title": "Help",
  "help.variable_text.p1": "Run a job many times with text that changes each time: a serial number counting up, or lines read from a spreadsheet file.",
  "help.variable_text.title": "Variable Text",
